==Description== <!--T:2-->

<!--T:3-->
This macro creates a customizable box with interlocked notches, designed for laser cutting or 3D printing. It allows you to specify box dimensions, material thickness, and notch parameters to generate a box that can be assembled without glue or screws.

==Usage== <!--T:4-->

<!--T:5-->
# Run the macro from the Macro menu
# A dialog will appear asking for box parameters:
#* **Width**: Inner width of the box
#* **Depth**: Inner depth of the box
#* **Height**: Inner height of the box
#* **Thickness**: Material thickness
#* **Notch Width**: Width of the interlocking notches
#* **Clearance**: Extra space for a tight fit
# Click **OK** to generate the box
# The box parts will be created as separate objects in the document

